# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values. .env is gitignored —
# .env.example is the only one of the two ever committed.
#
# This file is read two ways, both by design (see progress-tracker.md
# Architecture Decisions):
#   - Locally, by Deno scripts: `deno run --env-file=.env ...`
#   - Pushed to the deployed Edge Function's secret store:
#     `supabase secrets set --env-file=.env`
# Never reference these as VITE_-prefixed vars anywhere — Vite inlines any
# VITE_* var into the client bundle, which would ship a Gemini key inside
# the publicly-readable Chrome extension (invariant 2 / CLAUDE.md § Security
# rules explicitly forbids this).

# Single paid-tier Gemini key, read by agent-cycle/index.ts and passed to
# callModel(payload) as a one-element array (progress-tracker.md
# Architecture Decisions). The original design rotated 3 free-tier keys on
# quota/failure; that rotation was retired 2026-09-19 after gemini-2.5-flash
# started failing in production — callModel's own rotation loop is
# unchanged and still generalizes to N keys if this ever needs to grow
# again, so this stays a config change, not a code change.
GEMINI_API_KEY_1=

# CoinGecko Demo API key (2026-09-22) — optional but strongly recommended.
# Read by agent-cycle/, position-monitor/, and market-refresh/ (all three
# call into providers/coingecko.ts, which sends this as the
# x-cg-demo-api-key header on every request when present). Without it,
# every request falls back to CoinGecko's fully anonymous public endpoint,
# rate-limited to 5-15 calls/min SHARED across all of CoinGecko's
# worldwide anonymous traffic — trivially exceeded by one agent-cycle run
# alone (7 requests in one burst for 2 assets). A free Demo key raises
# this to a stable 100 calls/min + 10,000/month (register at
# coingecko.com/en/api/pricing, no card required) — that 10,000/month
# figure is this tier's, not the anonymous endpoint's.
COINGECKO_API_KEY=
